WHY THIS RUN MATTERS:
  The 3rd review found that verify_checksums.py split the manifest on
  CRLF only. The committed blob of CHECKSUMS.sha256 is LF, so an
  autocrlf=false checkout -- and every Linux / macOS checkout -- read
  the whole manifest as ONE line and reported a bogus MISMATCH
  (tracked-not-listed: 197). The previous round only ever verified
  the CRLF case.

